<BaseLayout title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="paper">
    <p>
      Hi, I am Shruti Chandra, a Master's student in Engineering Management at Tufts University,
      based in Boston and I am passionate in how research in accessibility, HCI, and systems thinking translates into real product decisions.
    </p>

    <p>
      This site is my ongoing journal of "what I think after reading", not just summaries.
      I write down what the paper argues, where I agree or disagree, and what it changes in my design lens.
    </p>

    <h2>What I've worked on</h2>
    <p>
      Most recently, I worked at Tulip Interfaces (User Research, Digital Marketing, and Operations Intern),
      where I analyzed qualitative and quantitative data across industries to surface user pain points,
      built automated data pipelines (n8n) that reduced manual input by 80%,
      and ran A/B testing and content analysis workflows to improve campaign performance.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before that, I was a Student Consultant with IBM, conducting mixed-methods usability research
      (contextual inquiry and user interviews) for voice and AR interactions and delivering recommendations
      that reduced cognitive load by 32%.
    </p>

    <p>
      I also worked at Deloitte India as a Business Analyst, where I designed and evaluated RLHF-based QA workflows
      for large-scale AI training (contributing to a 20% acceleration in model deployment),
      improved model accuracy by 30% through reinforcement-learning-based evaluation,
      and improved data accuracy by 30% by investigating 200+ ERP discrepancies.
    </p>

    <h2>Projects I care about</h2>
    <p>
      I like building and testing ideas end-to-end. My recent projects include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Prana (Next-Generation Asthma Care Solution):</strong> human-centered design research and iterative prototyping
        using AutoCAD, with a projected 65% improvement in adherence and $4.2M revenue.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shopaholics:</strong> 20+ interviews across 7 nationalities to a high-fidelity Figma prototype and feature prioritization.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Toolbox</h2>
    <p>
      User research (Figma, Dovetail, Maze, interviews, usability testing), data analysis (Python/pandas, SQL, Tableau, Power BI),
      automation (Zapier, n8n), and AI foundations (reinforcement learning, LLM evaluation).
    </p>

